detail.description_text:
Are you a caring, patient, and empathetic educator who believes every child deserves to thrive? We’re looking for a
Shadow Teacher
to provide one-on-one support to a student with special learning needs, helping them adapt, engage, and progress confidently in the classroom environment.
What you’ll do:
Support the child’s learning and behavior in a mainstream classroom setting;
Collaborate with classroom teachers and the school psychologist;
Help the student with focus, transitions, and social interactions;
Observe and report on progress and challenges;
Maintain discretion, compassion, and a student-centered approach.

detail.requirements_text:
What we’re looking for:
Experience working with children, especially those with learning differences;
Patience, emotional intelligence, and a growth mindset;
Strong communication and teamwork skills;
Background in education, psychology, or special education is a plus;
English is B1.
Note:
This role is tied to the needs of a specific student. Therefore, the duration of the position may vary, depending on the development and circumstances of the child’s learning journey. More details will be shared during the interview stage.
﻿
